This file documents the core logic used in the NorthStar Logistics dashboard.

1. Shipment Performance

On-Time Delivery % (OTD)
Calculates the percentage of orders delivered on or before the due date.

OTD % = 
VAR OnTimeShipments = 
    CALCULATE(
        DISTINCTCOUNT(Shipments[OrderID]),
        Shipments[DeliveryDate] <= Shipments[DueDate]
    )
VAR TotalShipments = DISTINCTCOUNT(Shipments[OrderID])
RETURN
    DIVIDE(OnTimeShipments, TotalShipments, 0)


2. Advanced Analytics

Top 3 Co-Shipped Products (Market Basket Analysis)
Identifies which products are frequently purchased alongside a selected item.
Logic: 1. Identify orders with selected item. 2. Calculate revenue of OTHER items in those orders.

Top 3 Co-Shipped Products = 
VAR TargetProduct = SELECTEDVALUE('Products'[ProductID])

-- Get list of Order IDs containing the selected product
VAR OrderWithTarget = 
    CALCULATETABLE(
        VALUES('Shipments_Data'[OrderID]), 
        'Products'[ProductID] = TargetProduct
    )

RETURN
    CALCULATE(
        [Total Revenue], 
        -- Filter for orders found in step 1
        'Shipments_Data'[OrderID] IN OrderWithTarget,
        -- Exclude the selected product itself
        'Products'[ProductID] <> TargetProduct,
        -- Remove filters to ensure other products are visible
        REMOVEFILTERS('Products') 
    )


3. Financial Simulation

Simulated Shipping Cost (What-If Parameter)
Allows users to adjust a slider to see the impact of rate increases.

Simulated Shipping Cost = 
VAR RateIncrease = 'Rate Increase %'[Rate Increase % Value]
RETURN
[Total Shipping Cost] * (1 + RateIncrease)


4. Inventory Health

Sell-Through Rate %
Used in the "Inventory Risk Matrix" scatter chart.

Sell-Through Rate % = 
VAR SalesQty = [Total Qty]
VAR StockQty = [Inv Qty Hand]
RETURN
DIVIDE(SalesQty, SalesQty + StockQty, 0)
